# COPIED-METHOD-DECLARED-FORMAL, the receiving contract of the selected callable: run's formal g, of contract getq
# (Wide: q; int: k), receives getq, getr (Other: q; ...) and getz (Zed: q; ...) -- signatures the structural rule
# admits.  The Wide w (pad 9, x 4) g is given is admitted to the model of the callable g holds and to no other: to
# Other by name, x being w's x and not its first place (b: 40 + 1), never to the contract's Wide or to Zed while g
# holds getq or getr.  While g holds getz the admission is refused where run forms the input, before the next actual
# tick() is evaluated, as run's implicit `implements`, which run's handler takes (77).  HEAD admitted to the contract
# and read Other's x at w's first place (b: 91).  tick() ran twice (tickcount reads the graph's cell).  Exit 7; 81 or 82
# otherwise.
Wide:
    int: pad 9
    int: x 4
end: Wide
Other:
    int: x 5
end: Other
Zed:
    int: z 6
    int: x 7
end: Zed
int: ticks 0
fn: tick () int
    node\ticks: node\ticks + 1
    return: 1
end: tick
fn: tickcount () int
    return: node\ticks
end: tickcount
fn: getq (Wide: q; int: k) int
    return: q\x + k
end: getq
fn: getr (Other: q; int: k) int
    return: q\x * 10 + k
end: getr
fn: getz (Zed: q; int: k) int
    return: q\z * 100 + k
end: getz
fn: run (getq: g; Wide: w) int
    int: r 0
    r: g(w; tick())
    catch: implements ()
        r: 77
    ---
    return: r
end: run
w: merge: Wide
int: a run(getq; w)
int: b run(getr; w)
int: c run(getz; w)
int: ok 7
if: a != 5 || b != 41 || c != 77
    ok: 81
if: tickcount() != 2
    ok: 82
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
